    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55130" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατασκέλλομαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>become a skeleton,
				wither away</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαρμάκων Χρείᾳ κατεσκέλλοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					481
				</span></i>
			: mostly in pf.
			
				Act.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατέσκληκα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				6.14.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Gall.</u>
				29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				8.7
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τῶν πόνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.19
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
			</span></i><i>Bis Acc.</i><i><span class="en">
				34
			</span></i>: plpf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμῶ κατεσκλήκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					46.8
				</span></i>
			; <i>to behard</i> or <i>frozen</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
			</span></i> l.c.: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-εσκληκώς</span>
			<i>austere</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.18.1
			</span></i>.</div>
